  "description": "Five Day Notification for tree works: Cherry tree at above property is dead and to be removed. Duty to replant Applies. , a replacement tree is to be planted in a suitable and convenient location within the front garden. The following three species are suggested for consideration:Amelanchier canadensis (Juneberry) Prunus sargentii (Pink flowering Cherry) Malus trilobata  (Lebanese Crab Apple). The replacement tree is to be planted during the October 2026 to March 2027 planting season, with a stem girth of between 8 to12 cm measured at 1 m above ground level and a minimum overall height of 2.5 m. The new tree should be securely supported with a suitable stake and tie to prevent wind-rock while the root system becomes established.",
